    <string name="help_storage_q">Where are my steps kept?</string>
    <string name="help_storage_a">On this phone. There is no account and no cloud.</string>
    <string name="help_permission_q">Why does Steply ask to recognize physical activity?</string>
    <string name="help_permission_a">To read the phone\'s step counter. If this permission is off, Data shows that collection is off.</string>
    <string name="help_background_q">Do steps still count when the app is closed?</string>
    <string name="help_background_a">Yes. Data shows whether collection is running and the time of the last reading.</string>
    <string name="help_goal_q">What is the daily goal?</string>
    <string name="help_goal_a">It starts at 8,000 steps. Set goal on Steps changes it. Goal notifications stay off until they are turned on in Settings. They remain on the phone: at most one notice on a day the goal is reached.</string>
    <string name="help_estimates_q">What are distance, time, and calories?</string>
    <string name="help_estimates_a">Estimates, not a medical measure. Weight and height are optional and only refine those estimates. The week count, such as 3/7, is how many days in that week reached the goal. It is not a streak.</string>
    <string name="help_units_q">What do units and language change?</string>
    <string name="help_units_a">Units change the display only. Distance, weight, and height stay stored in kilometers, kilograms, and centimeters. Language, appearance, and the accent color are in Settings and apply to the whole app.</string>
